{
	title: 'Opt-in local terminal repaint tracing',
	spec: 'Terminal repaint diagnostics are disabled by default and enabled explicitly from the terminal client home local.ts, including for hal -r. A browser or remote host setting never enables tracing on another machine. A small client-only module starts and stops tracing through existing mutable module-object hooks without changing renderer output, geometry, colors, timing policy, or emergency keys. Its owner-only local JSONL file records timestamps, process ID, initiating client event/heartbeat/keyboard/resize/redraw sources (including sources coalesced by the paint throttle), frame row counts, first changed row, writable boundary, force/fullscreen flags, cursor coordinates, and whether paint parts contain a scrollback clear or cursor-home. It distinguishes forced rebuilds, physical shrink, changes to immutable rows, ordinary diffs, and unchanged frames. Never record transcript text, tool arguments/results, keys typed, session names/IDs, URLs, credentials, hostnames, paths, or raw terminal bytes. Importing the module has no side effects; stopping restores owned hooks without overwriting subsequent replacements. Trace files reject symlinks and non-regular files, use mode 0600, and tracing stops at a bounded record count or on write failure without disrupting the terminal. Configuration instructions are generic examples in this task artifact; actual local configuration and trace output remain private and untracked. Behavioral tests verify default inertness, causal attribution, clear-vs-diff distinction, content exclusion, bounded logging, and hook cleanup.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The tracer wraps existing client module-object functions only when local.ts calls start. No app/render/main behavior or color code changes, and normal imports create no hooks or I/O. render.init installs terminal.redraw/onResize after local.ts loads, so tracing wraps render.init and attaches those callbacks afterward; tests cover this startup ordering. It records generated paint parts, not raw queued terminal writes or terminal-emulator viewport state.',
		'Validation: seven targeted behavioral tests and all six module-convention tests pass; targeted strict TypeScript and oxlint pass. The full shared-tree suite has unrelated failures (including process/restart timeouts and concurrent prompt/steering changes), so a clean full-suite result is not claimed.'
